{
  "id": "completion/templates/05_dependent_expression_results",
  "topic": "completion",
  "subtopic": "templates",
  "title": "Dependent expression results",
  "summary": "A member access on what a subscript or a member call returns inside a template completes the members of the class it evaluates to",
  "prose": "`rows[0].` on a `Vec<Vec<T>>` lists the members of `Vec<T>`, followed through the container's `reference` alias the way the standard containers declare it. Where a member has a `const` overload, the constness of the object picks the one called, a data member reached through a const object counting as const, and `->` on a returned iterator reaches the element.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#443"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "template <typename T>\nstruct Allocator {\n    using value_type = T;\n};\n\ntemplate <typename A>\nstruct AllocatorTraits {\n    using value_type = typename A::value_type;\n    using pointer = value_type*;\n};\n\ntemplate <typename P>\nstruct Iterator {\n    P operator->() const;\n};\n\ntemplate <typename T, typename A = Allocator<T>>\nstruct Vec {\n    using value_type = T;\n    using reference = value_type&;\n    using const_reference = const value_type&;\n    using iterator = Iterator<typename AllocatorTraits<A>::pointer>;\n\n    reference operator[](int index);\n    const_reference operator[](int index) const;\n    reference front();\n    const_reference front() const;\n    iterator begin();\n\n    void push_back(const T& value);\n    int size() const;\n};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Grid {\n    Vec<Vec<T>> rows;\n    mutable Vec<Vec<T>> cache;\n};\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nvoid bar(Vec<Vec<T>> rows, const Vec<Vec<T>>& fixed, const Grid<T>& grid) {\n    rows[0].;\n    rows.front().;\n    fixed[0].;\n    grid.rows.front().;\n    grid.cache.front().;\n    rows.begin()->;\n}\n",
